message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Orbital Rendezvous Simulator"
abstract: >-
  An open-source research and educational platform for spacecraft
  relative motion and rendezvous guidance. It implements the
  Clohessy-Wiltshire (Hill) linearised relative-motion equations with a
  Proportional-Derivative controller, and compares that linear model
  against a higher-fidelity non-linear orbital model (two-body plus J2
  oblateness plus atmospheric drag). The engine is deterministic
  fixed-step RK4 in SI units; the platform exposes it through a browser
  interface for students, teachers and researchers.
type: software
